    "seconds": 257,
    "summary": "The storefront is healthy again. The product-catalog failure came from the `productCatalogFailure` feature flag being on by default.\n\n**Root cause:** In the `flagd-config` ConfigMap, `productCatalogFailure` had `\"defaultVariant\": \"on\"`. Its default is supposed to be `off`. With it on, product `OLJCESPC7Z` returned HTTP 500 from product-catalog to every user, and the frontend and recommendations calls that depend on it failed too. The flagd and product-catalog pods were restarted at 17:42, but a restart doesn't change the flag value, so that wasn't the fix.\n\n**Change made:**\n- Set `productCatalogFailure.defaultVariant` to `\"off\"` in the `flagd-config` ConfigMap. No other flag was modified.\n- Restarted `flagd` so its init container re-copies the config, then restarted `product-catalog` so it picks up the new flag state.\n\n**Verification:**\n- `GET /api/products/OLJCESPC7Z` through frontend-proxy now returns 200 with product data (it returned 500 before).\n- `/api/recommendations` and the frontend homepage respond normally.\n- Every pod in `astronomy-shop` is Ready with no restarts.\n\n**Not changed:** `locust-fetcher` is an unusual pod, but it only polls the load generator's stats, so I left it alone. I didn't check the other flags' values against upstream beyond the ones I read.",
